{
  "id": "inferior-frontal-gyrus",
  "term": "inferior frontal gyrus",
  "definition": "The inferior frontal gyrus, especially on the left, is a frontal brain region that forms a central part of the language network. It includes subregions associated with speech production, sequencing of orofacial and other motor actions, syntactic processing, and controlled retrieval of meaning, and it connects with temporoparietal areas through dorsal and ventral pathways.",
